    ['Can you reuse my existing landscape lighting wire?', 'Sometimes. If the wire is in good condition and properly sized, it can often be reused with new LED fixtures, which typically reduces load. Damaged, undersized or poorly spliced wire is better replaced.'],
    ['Is it worth upgrading an old halogen system or starting over?', 'It depends on the layout. If fixture positions still make sense, converting to LED and fixing connections may be enough. If the design has glare, dark gaps or has been outgrown by the landscape, a redesign often gives a better result.'],
    ['Will installing lighting damage my mature trees?', 'Not when done carefully. We hand dig near major roots, avoid trenching through root zones where possible and use proper tree-mount hardware for any in-tree fixtures.'],
